(BUF-29: undocumented precision on OOB - a WRITE at an index within capacity but past current size succeeds and silently EXTENDS the buffer's length, zero-filling the gap, rather than erroring.)
(expected output:
4
6
0
88
)
a buffer called fx is 8 bytes in size.
append "ABCD" to fx.
print fx's size.
Set byte 6 of fx to 88.
print fx's size.
print byte 5 of fx.
print byte 6 of fx.
